<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e86490707719edbd882e4a418a739c8aeabc7d3f0b8a3d7c4d7a96b97c192412</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany beat Netherlands 5-0 to win Nations League group</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42b8ccf249f992f92a9e2110b5bf06d9c9f3cc905569b9f299966559a43bfc7b</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T23:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-beat-netherlands-5-0-to-win-nations-league-group/a-79964394--6bc86424ecf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-beat-netherlands-5-0-to-win-nations-league-group/a-79964394?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Florian Wirtz scored twice as Germany cruised to a comfortable 5-0 win over the Netherlands to qualify for the Nations League quarter-finals on Monday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:364dfff25dea55708f3fa0830298743c96547237aabba3c89aa39c2f66c2416b</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe01dd93f70ae9dce43fdb169888361b4012c167bfe19ea24ed7decde8202100</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp has said midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>France's Philippe Diallo to challenge Infantino for FIFA presidency</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d17b2b92195ec62c6befd287bb6bb84c0513c966561cbd85be930c1536b502d</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-philippe-diallo-to-challenge-infantino-for-fifa-presidency/a-79962843--6fe08ae5c0bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-philippe-diallo-to-challenge-infantino-for-fifa-presidency/a-79962843?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Philippe Diallo is the second candidate to stand against incumbent Gianni Infantino. He is backed by European football's governing body UEFA, known to be critical of Infantino.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey impasse as Russia threatens sanctions on Canada, Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed1523af7e6aae2b41a25fd13a0b1e571a77050c76395b930b67e027f6808ce2</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676--52aad908ad79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-impasse-as-russia-threatens-sanctions-on-canada-germany/a-79942676?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the CAS ordered ice hockey's governing body to reintegrate Russia into international play, a solution remains elusive. Now Russia has threatened to take legal action against two tournament hosts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8539a046af592025f58dea02da59c24afb210201ec578751465f5f0e69de1225</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88f8269025894ca782f1efc82a72a937875f0cfba57f5559eaecfba60986e913</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund's Felix Nmecha and the question of religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a51b88268bef8f82706ee52f5011fd825e183ea06faf5fce7c6b7ce075530ac</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432--cd7bb6e11389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Felix Nmecha's "Crowns down" celebration has drawn criticism from a Borussia Dortmund fan club, reopening debate over faith, inclusion and religious messaging in football.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's ice hockey team says Russia replacing it at World Juniors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:084452d2d2ec1ba44ec4d0ab013658b5dfa21ace8375390e03f13dcebbab99ee</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844--43300d3ba1be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-ice-hockey-team-says-russia-replacing-it-at-world-juniors/a-79901844?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The wrangling over Russia's return to international ice hockey continues, with Norway saying it has been kicked out of the next major tournament to accommodate Russia. Switzerland has joined a "boycott."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany hopes to host world ice hockey championship — without Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07063d4a79eaf56095e5e63d2f274c9920a6966789e20ff42776158669a6324e</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536--60661c53ebb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">International protests continue after a court ruled that Russia must be allowed to return to international ice hockey. Germany is seeking a solution that will allow the country to host next year's world championship.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russia is back in world sport, but who is drug testing its athletes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:919eae9649440771979717b4469ca28c76958582b4812310c7ab2b65c5b5f98b</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467--6f0e1f90efa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e12041533f118678ca4d05050817fcf719e681990a0232ced084e5cc7c6a7199</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1237a22e8b81991e3b4407416c4a01bf87911c2bfdca6aac23d15fcb186dcb9</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:44:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
